# GoldEx Project — AI Agent Rules

## Project Identity
This is GoldEx: a gold investment platform with daily profit, referral bonus, 
signup bonus, and USDT BEP20 deposits. Users want simplicity, trust, and 
clear profit visibility.

## Tech Stack
- React 18 + Vite + TypeScript (strict)
- TailwindCSS (utility-first, no custom CSS unless unavoidable)
- Framer Motion (animations only — no CSS keyframes for complex animations)
- Firebase Auth + Firestore (existing — do not replace)
- React Router v6 (existing routing)
- Recharts (existing charts — keep)

## Design System Rules
- Primary brand color: #D4AF37 (gold) — use as accent, not background
- Base background light mode: #FAFAF8
- Base background dark mode: #0F0F0E  
- Text primary: color-neutral-900 (light) / color-neutral-50 (dark)
- NEVER use glassmorphism backdrop-blur on primary content cards
- Card style: bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 rounded-2xl
- Success/profit: text-emerald-500 — ONLY for actual profit numbers
- Error/loss: text-red-500 — ONLY for actual negative values
- CTA buttons: bg-[#D4AF37] text-neutral-900 font-semibold rounded-xl

## Code Rules
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types
- All components as arrow functions: const ComponentName = () => {}
- Custom hooks start with `use` prefix
- All Firebase calls in /src/services/ directory only
- No inline styles — Tailwind classes only
- Every async function must have try/catch with proper error handling
- Mobile-first: design for 390px then scale up

## Folder Structure (enforce strictly)
src/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/           # Reusable: Button, Card, Input, Badge, Modal
│   ├── layout/       # Navbar, Sidebar, BottomNav, PageWrapper
│   └── features/     # Domain: Dashboard, Invest, Wallet, Referral
├── pages/            # Route-level components
├── hooks/            # Custom React hooks
├── services/         # Firebase + API calls only
├── stores/           # Zustand or Context stores
├── types/            # TypeScript interfaces
├── utils/            # Pure helper functions
└── assets/           # Static files

## What NOT to do
- Do NOT break existing Firebase Auth logic
- Do NOT remove existing Firestore data models
- Do NOT change environment variable names
- Do NOT add new npm packages without asking first
- Do NOT use `!important` in any styles
- Do NOT use `position: fixed` without explaining why
